# Worker-model override for the watch-loop dispatcher.
#
# This file is TEMPLATE — copy it into place as the LIVE config:
#     cp scripts/worker-model.template .watchloop/run/worker-model
# (.watchloop/ is gitignored, so the live config is a local, uncommitted file;
#  this template is tracked in git so the documented options are versioned.)
#
# Format (2 lines):
#   Line 1 = model id
#   Line 2 = provider name (leave blank for the profile default provider)
#
# Resolution order in scripts/watchloop_dispatch.py (`_read_worker_model_config`),
# high to low:
#   1. env WATCHLOOP_WORKER_MODEL / WATCHLOOP_WORKER_PROVIDER (crontab/export)
#   2. this config file (.watchloop/run/worker-model)
#   3. profile default (llm-local) if both are empty
#
# The spawned worker's `hermes chat` then launches with
# `-m <MODEL> --provider <PROVIDER>`.

# --- OPTION A: llama.cpp / local GGUF model (default; slow for agentic work) ---
# Serve a GGUF with the local llama-server then point workers at it. Empty lines
# make the dispatcher fall back to the profile default (llm-local). Leave MODEL
# blank / comment the next two lines to use the local model.
#
# NOTE (issue #37): when the effective provider is LOCAL (empty provider, or
# localhost/custom/llama.cpp), the dispatcher PROBES
# http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/models BEFORE spawning each worker and confirms the
# model id is listed. If the local llama-server is down (or hasn't finished
# loading), the spawn is SKIPPED cleanly — one log line per issue, no doomed
# worker, no lock, no worktree — and retried on the next 20-min tick.
# deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731  <- uncomment nothing; see OPTION B
# (for llama.cpp): set line 1 to `llm-local` and leave line 2 empty, e.g.:
#   llm-local
#   (blank provider => custom / localhost:11434)

# ------------------------------------------------------------ OPTION B: hosted (recommended for speed) ---
# Use a fast hosted model via OpenRouter. This is what makes the autonomous loop
# drive issues to a PR quickly instead of stalling on the local 35B (~170s/call).
deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731
openrouter
